    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough straddles Laurel Hill, a major north–south ridge of the Allegheny Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Springs%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Seven Springs is part of the Pittsburgh metropolitan area on the Fayette County side and the Johnstown metropolitan area on the Somerset County side.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Springs%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The borough limits cover most of the Seven Springs Mountain Resort, though the resort’s business address is listed as Champion, 7 miles northwest in Fayette County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Springs%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Because of its high elevation, Seven Springs feels like a cooler version of the surrounding climate, with winter temperatures often colder than Altoona or Johnstown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Springs%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
